==Russian==

===Etymology===
{{af|ru|про-|вести}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA|провести́}}
* {{audio|ru|Ru-провести.ogg}}
* {{homophones|ru|провезти́}}

===Verb===
{{ru-verb|провести́|pf|impf=проводи́ть}}

# to [[lead]], to [[conduct]], to [[guide]], to [[steer]], to [[take]]
# to [[lay]], to [[construct]], to [[build]], to [[install]] ''a road, a pipe, a wire etc.''
# to [[carry out]], to [[carry through]], to [[realize]], to [[put]] [[into]] [[practice]], to [[conduct]]
# to [[pass over]], to [[run over]]
# to [[spend]], to [[pass]] ''(time)''
#: {{uxi|ru|[[как|Как]] [[вы]] '''провели́''' [[вре́мя]]?|How was your time?}}
#* {{quote-book|ru|year=1869|author=w:ru:Лев Толстой<t:{{w|Leo Tolstoy}}>|title=w:ru:[[Война и мир]]|chapter=s:ru:[[Война_и_мир_(Толстой)/Том_2|Том 2, Часть третья, XXII]]|location=|publisher=|newversion=English translation from|translator2=w:en:Aylmer and Louise Maude|title2=s:en:[[War and Peace (Tolstoy)/Book 6/Chapter 22|War and Peace]]|location2=Oxford|publisher2=Oxford University Press|year2=1922–1923|page2=|pageurl2=|text=На друго́й день князь Андре́й пое́хал к Росто́вым обе́дать, так как его́ звал граф Илья́ Андре́ич, и '''провёл''' у них це́лый день.|t=Next day, having been invited by the count, Prince Andrew dined with the Rostóvs and '''spent''' the rest of the day there.}}
# to [[book]], to [[register]], to [[enter]]
# to [[draw]] ''a line''
# to [[cheat]], to [[take in]], to [[trick]], to [[fool]]

====Conjugation====
{{ru-conj|pf|7b/b(9)+p|провести́|провед|ёе}}

